      "threads": [
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Real yield vs volatile APY",
          "why": "Goldfinch's promise of stable 5% private-credit returns framed against the failure mode of token-incentive APYs gave readers a concrete, skepticism-satisfying contrast they could act on."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "CTO death, founder grief",
          "why": "The passing of cofounder Eugene Shen was the second-highest clicked story, showing Leviathan readers follow the human layer of crypto projects alongside the financial one."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Institutional vault products",
          "why": "EtherFi's Nest Vault via Superstate USCC and PIMCO/CMBI-backed fixed income on Bybit gave readers familiar TradFi brand names attached to onchain yield, making the products feel credible and accessible."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Regulatory milestone licensing",
          "why": "Bermuda's Digital Asset Licence positioned Plume as the first regulated vault operator, which clicked because it answered the compliance question that institutional and retail readers both carry about RWA platforms."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Tokenized payroll pilots",
          "why": "Converting employee wages into WisdomTree WTGXX shares represented a concrete, non-speculative use case that made tokenization tangible beyond trading."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "DeFi protocol integration + hack recovery",
          "why": "Curve going live on Plume and Plume's team assisting recovery of 857 pxETH in the yETH hack together showed readers the network is plugged into live DeFi risk, not just TradFi wrappers."
        }
      ]
    },
